#HSSS 1.0
TITLE: Ubuntu White Edition / Audit Specification
PACKAGE: audit
LANGUAGE: C, configuration
STATUS: W2
ROLE: Security event recording and accountability

## PROGRAM
Linux Audit records selected security-relevant events and provides evidence for operational review.

## STRUCTURE
SOURCE: upstream Linux Audit / Ubuntu package
BOUNDARY: kernel/security events -> audit rules -> daemon -> persistent records
WHITE_EDITION: baseline policy and observability overlay

## SPEC
- capture useful security events
- avoid redundant/high-volume noise
- define retention and rotation
- preserve useful evidence across normal service operation
- coordinate with AppArmor and systemd

## QUALITY
TEST: daemon startup, rule load, login/permission/process events, policy interaction, rotation, overload/noise, restart recovery
ECONOMY: event rate, disk growth, CPU, memory, useful-event ratio

## SOURCE POLICY
Prefer policy/configuration changes. Native changes require a concrete correctness/security requirement and dedicated tests.
